<title>USA: Sonic Corp board adopts rights plan.</title>
<headline>Sonic Corp board adopts rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>OKLAHOMA CITY, Okla. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sonic Corp said on Monday that its directors had adopted a stockholder rights plan to deter coercive takeover tactics.</p>
<p>Under the plan, common stock purchase rights will be distributed as a dividend at the rate of one right for each share of common stock, par value $0.01 per share, Sonic Corp said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plan applies to stockholders of record as of June 27, it added.</p>
<p>The drive-in restaurant farnchiser added that the rights plan is designed &quot;to prevent an acquiror from gaining control of the company without offering a fair price to all of the company's stockholders,&quot; and will expire on June 16, 2007.</p>
</text>
